# _t824-dist-immutability.sha256 — every released artefact, pinned.
#
# T-824. A release is a promise: version X means these exact bytes, forever (G-007).
# AEF vendors a dist/ artefact and verifies its sha256, so rewriting an already-released
# version breaks a consumer's pin with NO local signal — release-designer.sh's own guard
# fires only when IT is the thing doing the writing, and says nothing about a stray edit,
# a bad merge, or a well-meant reformat.
#
# Generated, never hand-edited. Regenerate ONLY when adding a newly-cut release:
#   cd /opt/832-Workflow-designer && sha256sum dist/aef-workflow-designer-*.html >> this file
# Changing an existing line here is changing the definition of a shipped version.
#
